diff --git a/internal/registerbot/README.md b/internal/registerbot/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0c262f6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/registerbot/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,195 @@
+# Registration engine
+
+`registerbot` adds persistent registration queues to the authenticated v8
+management API. The engine is initialized on the first registration API request;
+ordinary CPA startup does not launch Chrome. The first supplied driver is
+`freeaiapikey`. Multiple channel configurations can use that driver independently.
+
+## Queue and recovery
+
+- Input is one `account|password` pair per line. Empty lines and comments beginning
+  with `#` are ignored. Duplicate or malformed rows are reported as skipped.
+- A batch accepts up to 500 rows. The engine retains up to 100 runs and permits up
+  to 32 configured channels. Channel concurrency is bounded to 1-8 workers and
+  attempts to 1-10. The configured interval spaces account starts within a channel.
+- Transient driver failures retry up to `max-attempts`. Human verification becomes
+  `waiting_human` and does not block other queued rows. Import failures retain the
+  captured key in `pending_write`; resuming retries verification and the provider
+  write without registering the account again.
+- `pause` cancels current work and preserves its checkpoint. `resume` requeues
+  unfinished rows; `retry` also requeues failed rows. `cancel` removes unfinished
+  secrets and is terminal. Already committed provider keys are not rolled back.
+- On restart, unfinished runs are loaded as `paused`. Resuming is deliberate;
+  registration never restarts automatically after a process crash.
+- `target-keys: 0` processes all rows. A positive target reserves in-flight slots
+  to avoid excess automatic registrations. Once enough keys are committed,
+  unfinished rows without a captured key are skipped. Captured pending keys remain
+  recoverable rather than being discarded.
+
+## Local state
+
+The management adapter stores state in `registerbot/` next to the active CPA
+configuration file. It does not currently relocate this directory using the
+persisted `state-dir` setting.
+
+| File or directory | Contents |
+| --- | --- |
+| `settings.yaml` | Module settings and channel definitions; separate from CPA config |
+| `queue.enc` | AES-256-GCM encrypted queue credentials and pending captured keys |
+| `state.key` | Encryption key; protected with current-user DPAPI on Windows |
+| `events.jsonl` | Bounded, sanitized progress journal and replay sequence numbers |
+| `profiles/`, `browser-*.json`, `browser-*.pid` | Managed Chrome profiles and ownership records |
+| `evidence/` | Sanitized metadata when evidence capture is explicitly requested |
+
+On other platforms the encryption key uses owner-only file permissions. Queue
+and settings replacement uses a temporary file, file synchronization, and rename.
+Queue ciphertext is authenticated; a missing key or damaged ciphertext stops
+initialization rather than silently resetting the queue. Keep the queue and key
+together when backing up; Windows DPAPI recovery requires the same user context.
+
+Successful rows clear their password and full captured key. Failed or paused rows
+retain the encrypted information needed to retry. Browser profiles and settings
+are not encrypted by the queue store; a configured controller secret in
+`settings.yaml` remains local configuration data. Public snapshots contain masked
+accounts and key hints. Raw authentication pages and screenshots are not written
+by the evidence helper.
+
+## Gateway and browser behavior
+
+Gateway fallback is `controller -> proxy_only -> disabled`. Discovery tries an
+explicit controller first, then candidates derived from the forwarding port; the
+default proxy is `http://127.0.0.1:12450`, whose candidates include port `12440`.
+Controller failure keeps forwarding through the proxy. Forwarding failure selects
+direct connections. Manual keys and pending imports are probed again before
+verification, so they also use this fallback and can recover a restored proxy.
+
+A single Clash-compatible forwarding port has global selector state. The gateway
+therefore holds **one exclusive selector lease across all channels** for each
+automatic registration and its initial import. This serializes that portion of
+work even when channel concurrency is higher. `share-mode` does not create
+simultaneous independent per-channel exits. Node selection is confirmed against
+the controller; an observed exit IP does not establish that a node has an exclusive
+IP or prevent provider account restrictions. Human handoff releases the lease;
+resume attempts to pin the retained session's previous node again.
+
+Browser fallback is `embedded -> attach -> system -> manual`. Embedded and system
+modes use an installed Chrome/Chromium/Edge binary with an isolated profile, not a
+bundled browser download. A bounded pool reuses managed processes; each account
+gets a separate disposable browser context with its own forwarding setting.
+Attach mode requires a configured DevTools endpoint and does not take ownership
+of that browser process. Loopback debugging ports are allocated dynamically.
+
+Manual handoff retains the account page while CPA remains running. Complete the
+visible verification step and resume the run, or submit an obtained API key for
+verification and import. CAPTCHA, MFA, and other identity checks are not bypassed.
+On disconnect, disposable contexts close. A restart can recover a still-running
+owned browser only when its persisted browser endpoint UUID matches, but the
+account page checkpoint is not restored; unfinished registration resumes from the
+driver entry point. Graceful shutdown cancels workers, saves queue state, closes
+owned browsers, and disconnects attached browsers.
+
+## Defaults and settings
+
+The generated `settings.yaml` is authoritative. Representative active defaults:
+
+```yaml
+enabled: true
+gateway:
+  proxy-url: http://127.0.0.1:12450
+  share-mode: lease
+  verify-exit-ip: true
+  exit-ip-url: https://api.ipify.org?format=json
+  pin-timeout-seconds: 20
+  probe-timeout-seconds: 5
+browser:
+  mode: embedded
+  pool-size: 2
+  startup-timeout-seconds: 40
+  step-timeout-seconds: 120
+  retire-after: 8
+channels:
+  - id: freeaiapikey
+    kind: freeaiapikey
+    name: FreeAIapikey
+    enabled: true
+    provider: FreeAi
+    proxy-url: http://127.0.0.1:12450
+    concurrency: 1
+    group: 节点选择
+    rotate-node: true
+    interval-seconds: 45
+    step-delay-millis: 900
+    max-attempts: 2
+```
+
+Channel updates use the management API and require active account workers to be
+paused first. Other file settings are loaded at engine initialization; restart CPA
+after editing them. The schema retains some fields without an active runtime
+implementation: `gateway.auto-discover`, `gateway.circuit-*`,
+`browser.remote-debug-port`, and `browser.human-wait-seconds`. Discovery currently
+always considers its candidate list; manual handoff waits for an explicit action.
+The current FreeAI management importer uses the existing provider's canonical
+endpoint and always verifies, regardless of the schema's `import.*` fields.
+
+## Management API and events
+
+All routes below are relative to `/v8/management/registerbot` and use normal CPA
+management authentication. No credentials belong in an event-stream URL.
+
+| Method and path | Contract |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GET /` | Snapshot: channels, runs, counters, cursor, and storage-error flag |
+| `GET /channels` | Channel definitions |
+| `PUT /channels/:id` | Replace or create a channel definition |
+| `POST /runs` | `{ "channel": "freeaiapikey", "accounts": "..." }`; returns `{ "run": ... }` |
+| `POST /runs/:run/actions` | `{ "action": "pause|resume|retry|cancel" }` |
+| `POST /runs/:run/keys` | `{ "row_id": "...", "key": "..." }` |
+| `GET /gateway` | Last measured gateway status; no live probe |
+| `POST /gateway/probe` | Refresh gateway state |
+| `GET /events?after=N&channel=ID` | Authenticated SSE; channel filter is optional |
+
+SSE subscriptions capture replay and live subscription atomically. Entries use
+monotonic `id`/`seq` values; clients may also send `Last-Event-ID`. A trimmed or
+future cursor produces `reset`, followed by retained events. Slow subscribers are
+disconnected and must reconnect with their cursor. `ready` confirms subscription
+and comment heartbeats keep an otherwise idle connection active. The panel should
+refresh its snapshot when replay is reset; events are a bounded journal, not an
+unlimited audit history.
+
+Handlers expose fixed error codes such as `invalid_request`, `run_rejected`,
+`action_rejected`, `key_rejected`, and `engine_unavailable`, rather than upstream
+response bodies. Import stalls distinguish `verification_failed`,
+`provider_missing`, `config_conflict`, and `write_failed` when known.
+
+The FreeAI importer requires an existing, uniquely named `FreeAi` provider at
+`https://api.freeaiapikey.com/v1`. It checks the key with the models endpoint, then
+uses the same v8 configuration GET/PUT and ETag/If-Match contract as
+`providerKeyImport`. It preserves unrelated provider fields, avoids duplicate keys,
+and confirms the write by reading it back. The stored key entry retains the
+channel's `proxy-url`; the verification transport may temporarily be direct when
+the gateway has degraded.
+
+## Driver extension and verification
+
+Implement `Driver` (`Kind`, `Run`, and `Probe`), add its kind to
+`KnownChannelKinds`, and pass the driver to `NewEngine` or add it to the default
+factory. Use `Task.Report` for progress, `Task.OpenSession` for isolated sessions,
+and `ErrManualHandoff` for a retained human checkpoint. Return a `Harvest` only
+after obtaining the credential. Extend the management import adapter for any new
+provider family; it currently supports FreeAI's OpenAI-compatible destination.
+Update the panel's stage labels and all seven locales for new public stages.
+
+Use MoeForge JSON/regexp/base64 packages, structured logrus logging, and
+credential-acquisition-only time bounds. Never emit credentials or raw provider
+responses in events. Focused checks are:
+
+```sh
+go test ./internal/registerbot ./internal/api/handlers/management
+go vet ./internal/registerbot
+go build ./cmd/server
+```
+
+Unit tests exercise queue behavior, encrypted recovery, cancellation, gateway and
+browser isolation, replay, and provider write protection. They do not establish
+Google login success or external key usability. Full-suite and live end-to-end
+results must be recorded separately for the actual deployment.
diff --git a/internal/registerbot/browser.go b/internal/registerbot/browser.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..054d147
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/registerbot/browser.go
@@ -0,0 +1,821 @@
+package registerbot
+
+import (
+	"context"
+	"errors"
+	"fmt"
+	"io"
+	"net"
+	"os"
+	"os/exec"
+	"path/filepath"
+	"strings"
+	"sync"
+	"time"
+
+	"github.com/MoeForge/moego/json"
+	log "github.com/sirupsen/logrus"
+)
+
+// browserInstance is one pooled Chrome process plus its browser level CDP session.
+type browserInstance struct {
+	id        int
+	proc      *os.Process
+	control   *cdpClient
+	transport *cdpTransport
+	// port is the loopback DevTools endpoint; profileDir the isolated user data dir.
+	port       int
+	profileDir string
+	browser    string
+	mode       string
+	// used counts accounts this instance already served.
+	used     int
+	lastUsed time.Time
+	mu       sync.Mutex
+	pidFile  string
+	contexts int
+	proxyURL string
+	owned    bool
+	metaFile string
+}
+
+// Alive reports whether the instance can still drive a page.
+//
+// The DevTools HTTP endpoint is the liveness signal: Chrome closes it when the
+// process exits, so a answered /json/version means the instance is usable.
+func (b *browserInstance) Alive(ctx context.Context) bool {
+	if b == nil || b.transport == nil {
+		return false
+	}
+	if b.control != nil && b.control.loadErr() != nil {
+		return false
+	}
+	probeCtx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, 3*time.Second)
+	defer cancel()
+	_, errReady := b.transport.versionReady(probeCtx)
+	return errReady == nil
+}
+
+// ID identifies the pooled instance in events and evidence names.
+func (b *browserInstance) ID() int {
+	if b == nil {
+		return -1
+	}
+	return b.id
+}
+
+// Mode reports which ladder position produced this instance.
+func (b *browserInstance) Mode() string {
+	if b == nil {
+		return ""
+	}
+	return b.mode
+}
+
+// Browser describes the resolved build, for the panel header.
+func (b *browserInstance) Browser() string {
+	if b == nil {
+		return ""
+	}
+	return b.browser
+}
+
+// Used reports how many accounts this instance already served.
+func (b *browserInstance) Used() int {
+	if b == nil {
+		return 0
+	}
+	b.mu.Lock()
+	defer b.mu.Unlock()
+	return b.used
+}
+
+// ProfileDir returns the isolated user data directory of this instance.
+func (b *browserInstance) ProfileDir() string {
+	if b == nil {
+		return ""
+	}
+	return b.profileDir
+}
+
+// markUsed records one more served account.
+func (b *browserInstance) markUsed() {
+	if b == nil {
+		return
+	}
+	b.mu.Lock()
+	b.used++
+	b.lastUsed = time.Now()
+	b.mu.Unlock()
+}
+
+// Pool owns the embedded Chrome instances and the browser degradation ladder.
+//
+// The ladder is what guarantees the core capability keeps working:
+//
+//	embedded -> attach -> system -> manual
+//
+// embedded launches its own hidden Chrome with one isolated profile per pooled
+// instance, so a bulk run never multiplies the operator's own browser windows.
+// attach connects to a DevTools endpoint that is already listening. system reuses
+// the installed browser through the same CDP path with its own profile. manual
+// stops requiring a browser inside CPA and hands the step to the operator.
+type Pool struct {
+	settings func() Settings
+	stateDir string
+
+	mu        sync.Mutex
+	acquireMu sync.Mutex
+	instances map[int]*browserInstance
+	busy      map[int]bool
+	available chan struct{}
+	order     []int
+	nextID    int
+	mode      string
+	reason    string
+	proxyURL  string
+	recovered bool
+}
+
+// NewPool builds the browser pool. stateDir holds profiles and evidence.
+func NewPool(settingsFunc func() Settings, stateDir string) *Pool {
+	set := DefaultSettings()
+	if settingsFunc != nil {
+		set = settingsFunc()
+	}
+	return &Pool{
+		settings:  settingsFunc,
+		stateDir:  stateDir,
+		instances: make(map[int]*browserInstance),
+		busy:      make(map[int]bool),
+		available: make(chan struct{}, 1),
+		mode:      set.Browser.Mode,
+		proxyURL:  set.Gateway.ProxyURL,
+	}
+}
+
+// SetProxyURL selects forwarding for newly created isolated page contexts.
+func (p *Pool) SetProxyURL(proxyURL string) { p.mu.Lock(); p.proxyURL = proxyURL; p.mu.Unlock() }
+
+func (p *Pool) snapshotSettings() Settings {
+	if p == nil || p.settings == nil {
+		return DefaultSettings()
+	}
+	return p.settings()
+}
+
+// Mode reports the effective browser mode after any degradation.
+func (p *Pool) Mode() (string, string) {
+	p.mu.Lock()
+	defer p.mu.Unlock()
+	return p.mode, p.reason
+}
+
+// SetMode pins the ladder position, used by the panel override and by degradation.
+func (p *Pool) SetMode(mode, reason string) error {
+	switch mode {
+	case BrowserModeEmbedded, BrowserModeAttach, BrowserModeSystem, BrowserModeManual:
+	default:
+		return fmt.Errorf("registerbot: unknown browser mode %q", mode)
+	}
+	p.mu.Lock()
+	p.mode = mode
+	p.reason = reason
+	p.mu.Unlock()
+	return nil
+}
+
+// profileDir returns the isolated user data directory for one pooled instance.
+func (p *Pool) profileDir(id int) string {
+	set := p.snapshotSettings()
+	base := strings.TrimSpace(set.Browser.ProfileBaseDir)
+	if base == "" {
+		base = filepath.Join(p.stateDir, "profiles")
+	}
+	if !filepath.IsAbs(base) {
+		if abs, errAbs := filepath.Abs(base); errAbs == nil {
+			base = abs
+		}
+	}
+	return filepath.Join(base, fmt.Sprintf("instance-%d", id))
+}
+
+// freePort reserves a loopback port for one DevTools listener.
+func freePort() (int, error) {
+	listener, errListen := net.Listen("tcp", "127.0.0.1:0")
+	if errListen != nil {
+		return 0, errListen
+	}
+	addr, ok := listener.Addr().(*net.TCPAddr)
+	port := 0
+	if ok {
+		port = addr.Port
+	}
+	if errClose := listener.Close(); errClose != nil {
+		_ = errClose
+	}
+	if port == 0 {
+		return 0, errors.New("registerbot: devtools port allocation failed")
+	}
+	return port, nil
+}
+
+// launchArgs builds the Chrome command line for one pooled instance.
+func launchArgs(set Settings, profileDir string, port int) []string {
+	width, height := set.Browser.WindowWidth, set.Browser.WindowHeight
+	if width <= 0 {
+		width = 1440
+	}
+	if height <= 0 {
+		height = 900
+	}
+	args := []string{
+		fmt.Sprintf("--remote-debugging-port=%d", port),
+		"--remote-debugging-address=127.0.0.1",
+		"--user-data-dir=" + profileDir,
+		fmt.Sprintf("--window-size=%d,%d", width, height),
+		"--window-position=80,80",
+		"--no-first-run",
+		"--no-default-browser-check",
+		"--disable-background-networking",
+		"--disable-component-update",
+		"--disable-sync",
+		"--disable-features=Translate,MediaRouter",
+		"--disable-session-crashed-bubble",
+		"--disable-infobars",
+		"--no-service-autorun",
+		"--password-store=basic",
+		"--test-type",
+		"--lang=en-US",
+	}
+	if set.Browser.Headless {
+		args = append(args, "--headless=new", "--disable-gpu")
+	}
+	if proxyURL := strings.TrimSpace(set.Gateway.ProxyURL); proxyURL != "" {
+		args = append(args, "--proxy-server="+proxyURL)
+	}
+	args = append(args, set.Browser.ExtraArgs...)
+	return append(args, "about:blank")
+}
+
+// resolveChrome returns the first existing configured browser binary.
+func (p *Pool) resolveChrome() (string, error) {
+	set := p.snapshotSettings()
+	for _, candidate := range set.Browser.ChromePaths {
+		candidate = strings.TrimSpace(candidate)
+		if candidate == "" {
+			continue
+		}
+		if stat, errStat := os.Stat(candidate); errStat == nil && !stat.IsDir() {
+			return candidate, nil
+		}
+	}
+	for _, name := range []string{"chrome", "chrome.exe", "chromium", "msedge"} {
+		if found, errLook := exec.LookPath(name); errLook == nil {
+			return found, nil
+		}
+	}
+	return "", errors.New("registerbot: no Chrome/Chromium/Edge binary found")
+}
+
+// poolSize returns the configured live instance ceiling.
+func (p *Pool) poolSize() int {
+	size := p.snapshotSettings().Browser.PoolSize
+	if size <= 0 {
+		return 1
+	}
+	if size > 8 {
+		return 8
+	}
+	return size
+}
+
+// Acquire hands out a live instance, launching one when the pool is short.
+func (p *Pool) Acquire(ctx context.Context) (*browserInstance, error) {
+	for {
+		instance, errAcquire := p.tryAcquire(ctx)
+		if !errors.Is(errAcquire, errPoolBusy) {
+			return instance, errAcquire
+		}
+		select {
+		case <-ctx.Done():
+			return nil, ctx.Err()
+		case <-p.available:
+		}
+	}
+}
+
+var errPoolBusy = errors.New("registerbot: browser pool busy")
+
+func (p *Pool) tryAcquire(ctx context.Context) (*browserInstance, error) {
+	p.acquireMu.Lock()
+	defer p.acquireMu.Unlock()
+	if !p.recovered {
+		p.recovered = true
+		p.recoverManaged(ctx)
+	}
+	set := p.snapshotSettings()
+	p.mu.Lock()
+	mode := p.mode
+	p.mu.Unlock()
+
+	if mode == BrowserModeManual {
+		return nil, ErrManualHandoff
+	}
+
+	// Reuse a live instance whose usage budget is not exhausted.
+	for _, instance := range p.liveInstances() {
+		p.mu.Lock()
+		busy := p.busy[instance.id]
+		p.mu.Unlock()
+		if busy {
+			continue
+		}
+		instance.mu.Lock()
+		contexts := instance.contexts
+		instance.mu.Unlock()
+		if contexts == 0 && set.Browser.RetireAfter > 0 && instance.Used() >= set.Browser.RetireAfter {
+			p.retire(instance)
+			continue
+		}
+		if instance.Alive(ctx) {
+			instance.markUsed()
+			p.mu.Lock()
+			p.busy[instance.id] = true
+			instance.mu.Lock()
+			instance.proxyURL = p.proxyURL
+			instance.mu.Unlock()
+			p.mu.Unlock()
+			return instance, nil
+		}
+		p.retire(instance)
+	}
+
+	if len(p.liveInstances()) >= p.poolSize() {
+		return nil, errPoolBusy
+	}
+
+	rungs := []string{BrowserModeEmbedded, BrowserModeAttach, BrowserModeSystem}
+	for i, rung := range rungs {
+		if rung == mode {
+			rungs = rungs[i:]
+			break
+		}
+	}
+	var lastErr error
+	seen := make(map[string]bool, len(rungs))
+	for _, rung := range rungs {
+		if rung == BrowserModeManual || seen[rung] {
+			continue
+		}
+		seen[rung] = true
+		instance, errLaunch := p.launchAs(ctx, set, rung)
+		if errLaunch == nil {
+			if rung != mode {
+				_ = p.SetMode(rung, fmt.Sprintf("browser degraded from %s to %s: %v", mode, rung, lastErr))
+				log.WithFields(log.Fields{"from": mode, "to": rung, "cause": errString(lastErr)}).
+					Warn("registerbot: browser ladder degradation")
+			}
+			instance.markUsed()
+			p.mu.Lock()
+			p.busy[instance.id] = true
+			instance.mu.Lock()
+			instance.proxyURL = p.proxyURL
+			instance.mu.Unlock()
+			p.mu.Unlock()
+			return instance, nil
+		}
+		lastErr = errLaunch
+	}
+	// Nothing can provide a browser: keep the batch alive by handing steps to the
+	// operator instead of failing the whole run.
+	_ = p.SetMode(BrowserModeManual, "browser ladder exhausted: "+errString(lastErr))
+	return nil, ErrManualHandoff
+}
+
+// Release returns an exclusive process slot while retaining manual page contexts.
+func (p *Pool) Release(instance *browserInstance) {
+	if instance == nil {
+		return
+	}
+	p.mu.Lock()
+	delete(p.busy, instance.id)
+	p.mu.Unlock()
+	select {
+	case p.available <- struct{}{}:
+	default:
+	}
+}
+
+// launchAs starts one instance forced to a specific ladder position.
+func (p *Pool) launchAs(ctx context.Context, set Settings, mode string) (*browserInstance, error) {
+	switch mode {
+	case BrowserModeEmbedded, BrowserModeSystem:
+		return p.launchProcess(ctx, set, mode)
+	case BrowserModeAttach:
+		return p.attach(ctx, set)
+	default:
+		return nil, fmt.Errorf("registerbot: mode %q does not provide a browser", mode)
+	}
+}
+
+// launchProcess starts a local browser binary and waits for its DevTools endpoint.
+func (p *Pool) launchProcess(ctx context.Context, set Settings, mode string) (*browserInstance, error) {
+	exe, errResolve := p.resolveChrome()
+	if errResolve != nil {
+		return nil, errResolve
+	}
+	port, errPort := freePort()
+	if errPort != nil {
+		return nil, errPort
+	}
+	p.mu.Lock()
+	id := p.nextID
+	p.nextID++
+	p.mu.Unlock()
+
+	profileDir := p.profileDir(id)
+	if errMkdir := os.MkdirAll(profileDir, 0o700); errMkdir != nil {
+		return nil, fmt.Errorf("registerbot: create profile dir: %w", errMkdir)
+	}
+
+	cmd := exec.Command(exe, launchArgs(set, profileDir, port)...)
+	hideWindow(cmd)
+	stdout, errStdout := cmd.StdoutPipe()
+	if errStdout != nil {
+		return nil, fmt.Errorf("registerbot: browser stdout pipe: %w", errStdout)
+	}
+	stderr, errStderr := cmd.StderrPipe()
+	if errStderr != nil {
+		_ = stdout.Close()
+		return nil, fmt.Errorf("registerbot: browser stderr pipe: %w", errStderr)
+	}
+	if errStart := cmd.Start(); errStart != nil {
+		_ = stdout.Close()
+		_ = stderr.Close()
+		return nil, fmt.Errorf("registerbot: launch browser: %w", errStart)
+	}
+	go drainBrowserLog(stdout, id)
+	go drainBrowserLog(stderr, id)
+
+	instance := &browserInstance{
+		id:         id,
+		proc:       cmd.Process,
+		port:       port,
+		profileDir: profileDir,
+		transport:  newCDPTransport(fmt.Sprintf("127.0.0.1:%d", port)),
+		browser:    filepath.Base(exe),
+		mode:       mode,
+		owned:      true,
+		lastUsed:   time.Now(),
+	}
+	if instance.proc != nil {
+		instance.pidFile = filepath.Join(p.stateDir, fmt.Sprintf("browser-%d.pid", id))
+		_ = os.WriteFile(instance.pidFile, []byte(fmt.Sprint(instance.proc.Pid)), 0o600)
+	}
+
+	waitCtx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, set.Browser.StartupTimeout())
+	defer cancel()
+	if errWait := waitForDevTools(waitCtx, instance.transport); errWait != nil {
+		instance.shutdown()
+		return nil, errWait
+	}
+	controlCtx, controlCancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, 10*time.Second)
+	defer controlCancel()
+	control, errConnect := instance.transport.connectBrowser(controlCtx)
+	if errConnect != nil {
+		instance.shutdown()
+		return nil, errConnect
+	}
+	instance.control = control
+	instance.metaFile = filepath.Join(p.stateDir, fmt.Sprintf("browser-%d.json", id))
+	meta := managedBrowser{ID: id, Port: port, Browser: instance.browser, Mode: mode, Endpoint: control.endpoint, ProfileDir: profileDir}
+	if encoded, errEncode := json.Marshal(meta); errEncode == nil {
+		if errWrite := os.WriteFile(instance.metaFile+".tmp", encoded, 0o600); errWrite == nil {
+			_ = os.Rename(instance.metaFile+".tmp", instance.metaFile)
+		}
+	}
+	if version, errVersion := instance.transport.versionReady(controlCtx); errVersion == nil && version != "" {
+		instance.browser = version
+	}
+
+	p.mu.Lock()
+	p.instances[id] = instance
+	p.order = append(p.order, id)
+	p.mu.Unlock()
+	log.WithFields(log.Fields{
+		"instance": id, "mode": mode, "port": port, "profile": profileDir,
+	}).Debug("registerbot: browser instance ready")
+	return instance, nil
+}
+
+// attach connects to a DevTools endpoint that is already listening.
+func (p *Pool) attach(ctx context.Context, set Settings) (*browserInstance, error) {
+	endpoint := strings.TrimSpace(set.Browser.AttachURL)
+	if endpoint == "" {
+		return nil, errors.New("registerbot: no attach endpoint configured")
+	}
+	transport := newCDPTransport(endpoint)
+	waitCtx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, 5*time.Second)
+	defer cancel()
+	if errWait := waitForDevTools(waitCtx, transport); errWait != nil {
+		return nil, errWait
+	}
+	controlCtx, controlCancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, 10*time.Second)
+	defer controlCancel()
+	control, errConnect := transport.connectBrowser(controlCtx)
+	if errConnect != nil {
+		return nil, errConnect
+	}
+	p.mu.Lock()
+	id := p.nextID
+	p.nextID++
+	p.mu.Unlock()
+	instance := &browserInstance{
+		id: id, control: control, transport: transport,
+		browser: "attached endpoint", mode: BrowserModeAttach, lastUsed: time.Now(),
+	}
+	p.mu.Lock()
+	p.instances[id] = instance
+	p.order = append(p.order, id)
+	p.mu.Unlock()
+	return instance, nil
+}
+
+// waitForDevTools polls a DevTools endpoint until it answers.
+func waitForDevTools(ctx context.Context, transport *cdpTransport) error {
+	ticker := time.NewTicker(300 * time.Millisecond)
+	defer ticker.Stop()
+	var lastErr error
+	for {
+		probeCtx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, 2*time.Second)
+		_, lastErr = transport.versionReady(probeCtx)
+		cancel()
+		if lastErr == nil {
+			return nil
+		}
+		select {
+		case <-ctx.Done():
+			return fmt.Errorf("registerbot: devtools endpoint did not come up: %v (last: %v)", ctx.Err(), lastErr)
+		case <-ticker.C:
+		}
+	}
+}
+
+// drainBrowserLog forwards browser output to debug logs only, never to the
+// account event stream, so tokens in URLs cannot leak into the panel.
+func drainBrowserLog(reader io.Reader, id int) {
+	// Browser diagnostics may contain URLs or page data. Drain without logging.
+	_, _ = io.Copy(io.Discard, reader)
+}
+
+func redactBrowserLine(text string) string {
+	if len(text) > 400 {
+		return text[:400] + "..."
+	}
+	return text
+}
+
+// liveInstances returns pooled instances in launch order.
+func (p *Pool) liveInstances() []*browserInstance {
+	p.mu.Lock()
+	defer p.mu.Unlock()
+	out := make([]*browserInstance, 0, len(p.order))
+	for _, id := range p.order {
+		if instance := p.instances[id]; instance != nil {
+			out = append(out, instance)
+		}
+	}
+	return out
+}
+
+// retire drops one instance from the pool and stops it.
+func (p *Pool) retire(instance *browserInstance) {
+	if instance == nil {
+		return
+	}
+	p.mu.Lock()
+	delete(p.instances, instance.id)
+	delete(p.busy, instance.id)
+	for i, id := range p.order {
+		if id == instance.id {
+			p.order = append(p.order[:i], p.order[i+1:]...)
+			break
+		}
+	}
+	p.mu.Unlock()
+	if errStop := instance.shutdown(); errStop != nil {
+		log.WithError(errStop).Debug("registerbot: instance shutdown reported an error")
+	}
+}
+
+// Retire marks an instance for restart, used after a hard page stall.
+func (p *Pool) Retire(instance *browserInstance) {
+	p.retire(instance)
+}
+
+// Shutdown stops every pooled instance.
+func (p *Pool) Shutdown() error {
+	var firstErr error
+	for _, instance := range p.liveInstances() {
+		p.retire(instance)
+	}
+	p.mu.Lock()
+	p.instances = make(map[int]*browserInstance)
+	p.order = nil
+	p.mu.Unlock()
+	return firstErr
+}
+
+// PoolStatus is the pool view exposed to the panel.
+type PoolStatus struct {
+	Mode       string           `json:"mode"`
+	Reason     string           `json:"reason,omitempty"`
+	PoolSize   int              `json:"pool_size"`
+	Live       int              `json:"live"`
+	Headless   bool             `json:"headless"`
+	Instances  []InstanceStatus `json:"instances"`
+	Candidates []string         `json:"chrome_candidates,omitempty"`
+	Ladder     []LadderStep     `json:"ladder"`
+}
+
+// InstanceStatus describes one live browser instance.
+type InstanceStatus struct {
+	ID       int    `json:"id"`
+	PID      int    `json:"pid,omitempty"`
+	Port     int    `json:"port,omitempty"`
+	Browser  string `json:"browser,omitempty"`
+	Mode     string `json:"mode,omitempty"`
+	Used     int    `json:"used"`
+	Attached bool   `json:"attached"`
+}
+
+// LadderStep is one ladder position with its measured readiness.
+type LadderStep struct {
+	Mode  string `json:"mode"`
+	Ready bool   `json:"ready"`
+	Note  string `json:"note,omitempty"`
+}
+
+// Status summarises the pool and probes every ladder position.
+func (p *Pool) Status(ctx context.Context) PoolStatus {
+	set := p.snapshotSettings()
+	mode, reason := p.Mode()
+	instances := p.liveInstances()
+	status := PoolStatus{
+		Mode:       mode,
+		Reason:     reason,
+		PoolSize:   p.poolSize(),
+		Live:       len(instances),
+		Headless:   set.Browser.Headless,
+		Candidates: set.Browser.ChromePaths,
+	}
+	for _, instance := range instances {
+		item := InstanceStatus{
+			ID: instance.id, Port: instance.port, Browser: instance.browser,
+			Mode: instance.mode, Used: instance.Used(), Attached: instance.proc == nil && !instance.owned,
+		}
+		if instance.proc != nil {
+			item.PID = instance.proc.Pid
+		}
+		status.Instances = append(status.Instances, item)
+	}
+	_, errResolve := p.resolveChrome()
+	browserFound := errResolve == nil
+	for _, rung := range []string{BrowserModeEmbedded, BrowserModeAttach, BrowserModeSystem, BrowserModeManual} {
+		entry := LadderStep{Mode: rung}
+		switch rung {
+		case BrowserModeEmbedded:
+			entry.Ready = browserFound
+			if !browserFound {
+				entry.Note = "no local Chrome binary"
+			}
+		case BrowserModeAttach:
+			probeCtx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, 2*time.Second)
+			_, errReady := newCDPTransport(set.Browser.AttachURL).versionReady(probeCtx)
+			cancel()
+			entry.Ready = errReady == nil
+			if !entry.Ready {
+				entry.Note = "no DevTools endpoint at " + set.Browser.AttachURL
+			}
+		case BrowserModeSystem:
+			entry.Ready = browserFound
+		case BrowserModeManual:
+			entry.Ready = true
+			entry.Note = "operator completes the step in their own window"
+		}
+		status.Ladder = append(status.Ladder, entry)
+	}
+	return status
+}
+
+// kill stops the process without a graceful CDP close.
+func (b *browserInstance) kill() {
+	if b == nil {
+		return
+	}
+	if b.control != nil && b.proc != nil {
+		_ = b.control.Close()
+		b.control = nil
+	}
+	if b.control != nil {
+		_ = b.control.Close()
+		b.control = nil
+	}
+	if b.proc != nil {
+		_ = b.proc.Kill()
+		_, _ = b.proc.Wait()
+		b.proc = nil
+	}
+	if b.pidFile != "" {
+		_ = os.Remove(b.pidFile)
+	}
+}
+
+// shutdown asks the browser to exit gracefully, then kills it.
+func (b *browserInstance) shutdown() error {
+	if b == nil {
+		return nil
+	}
+	var errCall error
+	if b.control != nil {
+		if b.proc != nil || b.owned {
+			ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 3*time.Second)
+			_, errCall = b.control.Call(ctx, "Browser.close", nil)
+			cancel()
+		}
+		_ = b.control.Close()
+		b.control = nil
+	}
+	if b.proc != nil {
+		waited := make(chan struct{})
+		go func() {
+			defer close(waited)
+			_, _ = b.proc.Wait()
+		}()
+		timer := time.NewTimer(2 * time.Second)
+		defer timer.Stop()
+		select {
+		case <-waited:
+		case <-timer.C:
+			_ = b.proc.Kill()
+			<-waited
+		}
+		b.proc = nil
+	}
+	if b.pidFile != "" {
+		_ = os.Remove(b.pidFile)
+	}
+	if b.metaFile != "" {
+		_ = os.Remove(b.metaFile)
+	}
+	return errCall
+}
+
+type managedBrowser struct {
+	ID         int    `json:"id"`
+	Port       int    `json:"port"`
+	Browser    string `json:"browser"`
+	Mode       string `json:"mode"`
+	Endpoint   string `json:"endpoint"`
+	ProfileDir string `json:"profile_dir"`
+}
+
+// recoverManaged reconnects only an endpoint whose browser UUID still matches
+// our persisted ownership record; a reused port cannot become an owned browser.
+func (p *Pool) recoverManaged(ctx context.Context) {
+	paths, _ := filepath.Glob(filepath.Join(p.stateDir, "browser-*.json"))
+	for _, path := range paths {
+		data, errRead := os.ReadFile(path)
+		if errRead != nil {
+			continue
+		}
+		var meta managedBrowser
+		if json.Unmarshal(data, &meta) != nil || meta.Port < 1 || meta.Port > 65535 || meta.Endpoint == "" {
+			continue
+		}
+		if meta.ID >= p.nextID {
+			p.nextID = meta.ID + 1
+		}
+		transport := newCDPTransport(fmt.Sprintf("127.0.0.1:%d", meta.Port))
+		probeCtx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, 2*time.Second)
+		var version struct {
+			Endpoint string `json:"webSocketDebuggerUrl"`
+		}
+		errVersion := transport.getJSON(probeCtx, "/json/version", &version)
+		if errVersion != nil || version.Endpoint != meta.Endpoint {
+			cancel()
+			continue
+		}
+		control, errConnect := transport.connectBrowser(probeCtx)
+		cancel()
+		if errConnect != nil {
+			continue
+		}
+		instance := &browserInstance{id: meta.ID, port: meta.Port, mode: meta.Mode, browser: meta.Browser, profileDir: meta.ProfileDir, control: control, transport: transport, owned: true, metaFile: path, proxyURL: p.proxyURL}
+		p.mu.Lock()
+		p.instances[meta.ID] = instance
+		p.order = append(p.order, meta.ID)
+		p.mu.Unlock()
+	}
+}
